# Commits that changed formatting (line endings, lint) and nothing else.
# `git blame` on any file they touched would otherwise point here instead of
# at the change that last touched the content.
#
# GitHub applies this file automatically in its blame view. Locally it is
# opt-in, once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Adding it is what stops the next person mistaking a normalisation for
# authorship. New CRLF churn should not happen again — .gitattributes pins the
# stored form to LF — so this file should stay short.

